  "plan": {
    "goal": "Reproduce physiological brain microvascular endothelial shear (0.5 Pa) in a perfused BBB channel using hCMEC/D3 cells.",
    "rationale": "Brain microvascular endothelial cells experience capillary shear in the ~0.1-1 Pa range (microvascular endothelium convention, consistent with HUVEC registry shear 0.1-1 Pa). I target the midpoint, 0.5 Pa (5 dyn/cm²), which is a commonly cited physiological brain capillary shear. For a 400 µm × 100 µm rectangular channel, the flow-rate-for-shear calculator gives 20 µL/min at 0.5 Pa (viscosity 0.001 Pa·s, water-like culture medium). This yields Re ≈ 1.3 (firmly laminar), residence time ≈ 2.4 s over a 20 mm channel, and a pressure drop of ~200 Pa — all well within syringe-pump capability. hCMEC/D3 is seeded at 20,000 cells/cm² (upper endothelial range) onto the 0.08 cm² channel floor = 1600 cells. Caveat: hCMEC/D3 forms only a moderately restrictive barrier (model TEER 100-240 Ω·cm² vs 1800-2000 Ω·cm² physiological BBB); the chip reproduces physiological shear but cannot reach in-vivo BBB TEER with this line alone.",
